 "intro": {
  "cards": [
   {
    "title": "What it is",
    "body": "Present simple is for **habits**, **routines**, and **facts** — not only “right now”.",
    "table": {
     "headers": [
      "Use",
      "Example"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "habit / routine",
       "I **work** every day."
      ],
      [
       "fact",
       "Water **boils** at 100°C."
      ],
      [
       "with time words",
       "She **goes** on Mondays."
      ]
     ]
    }
   },
   {
    "title": "Form",
    "table": {
     "headers": [
      "Subject",
      "positive",
      "negative"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "I / you / we / they",
       "work",
       "don't work"
      ],
      [
       "he / she / it",
       "works",
       "doesn't work"
      ]
     ]
    },
    "points": [
     "he/she/it → **-s** in the positive: works · likes · goes · has",
     "Negatives: see next card"
    ]
   },
   {
    "title": "Negatives",
    "body": "Use **do / does** + **not** + base verb. Short forms are common in speech.",
    "table": {
     "headers": [
      "Subject",
      "negative",
      "short"
     ],
     "rows": [
      [
       "I / you / we / they",
       "do not work",
       "don't work"
      ],
      [
       "he / she / it",
       "does not work",
       "doesn't work"
      ]
     ]
    },
    "points": [
     "After *don't / doesn't*, the main verb has **no -s**: She doesn't **work** (not *works*)",
     "he/she/it → **doesn't** · I/you/we/they → **don't**",
     "Not: *She not work* · *He don't like*"
    ]
   },
   {
    "title": "When",
    "table": {
